### DynamoDB Single-Table Model
// | PK | SK | Type | Order | Details | DeletedAt |
// | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
// | USER#U1 | CREDENTIALS | | | { user="U1", hash="$1$2$3" } | |
// | USER#U1 | GOAL#2026-10-04 | | | { k=2000, p=150, c=200, f=60 } | |
// | USER#U1 | CATALOG#a1a1a1 | MEAL | 1 | {"item":{"label":"almonds","k":579,"p":21,"c":22,"f":50}} | |
// | USER#U1 | CATALOG#b2b2b2 | MEAL | 2 | {"item":{"label":"yogurt","k":61,"p":4,"c":5,"f":4}} | |
// | USER#U1 | LOG#2026-10-04#c3c3c3 | MEAL | 1 | {"item":{"label":"almonds","k":579,"p":21,"c":22,"f":50}} | |
// | USER#U1 | LOG#2026-10-04#d4d4d4 | MEAL | 2 | {"item":{"label":"yogurt","k":61,"p":4,"c":5,"f":4}} | |
### DOCUMENTACION Request/Response (FUENTE DE LA VERDAD - EJEMPLOS):
// 1. POST /logs?date=2026-10-04
// POST { "MEAL": { "label": "100g almonds", "k": 579, "p": 21, "c": 22, "f": 50 } }
// 201 Created
// { "OK": true, "SK": "LOG#YYYY-MM-DD#a1a1a1" }
// 2. GET /logs?date=2026-10-04
// 200 OK
// [
//   { "type": "MEAL", "label": "almonds", "k": 579, "p": 21, "c": 22, "f": 50 },
//   { "type": "MEAL", "label": "yogurt", "k": 61, "p": 4, "c": 5, "f": 4}
// ]
// 3. PATCH /logs
// PATCH { "SK": "LOG#YYYY-MM-DD#a1a1a1" }
// 200 OK
// { "OK": true, "SK": "LOG#YYYY-MM-DD#a1a1a1", "DeletedAt": "2026-10-04T20:44:00" }
// 4. POST /catalog?date=2026-10-04
// POST { "MEAL": { "label": "100g almonds", "k": 579, "p": 21, "c": 22, "f": 50 } }
// 201 Created
// { "OK": true, "SK": "CATALOG#a1a1a1" }
// 5. GET /catalog?date=2026-10-04
// 200 OK
// [
//   { "type": "MEAL", "label": "almonds", "k": 579, "p": 21, "c": 22, "f": 50 },
//   { "type": "MEAL", "label": "yogurt", "k": 61, "p": 4, "c": 5, "f": 4}
// ]
// 6. PATCH /catalog
// PATCH { "SK": "CATALOG#a1a1a1" }
// 200 OK
// { "OK": true, "SK": "CATALOG#a1a1a1", "DeletedAt": "2026-10-04T20:33:00" }

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/v1
@date1 = 2026-10-06
@date2 = 2026-10-07

### 1. POST : Log a meal for a selected date
POST {{baseUrl}}/logs?date={{date1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "MEAL": { "label": "100g orange", "k": 579, "p": 21, "c": 22, "f": 50 }
}

### 2. GET : Get logs for that date
GET {{baseUrl}}/logs?date={{date1}}

### 2.b GET : Get logs for another date
GET {{baseUrl}}/logs?date={{date2}}

### 3. PATCH : Soft-delete a log entry (use the SK returned by POST)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/logs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "SK": "LOG#2026-10-05#a1a1a1"
}

### 4. POST : Add a meal to the catalog
POST {{baseUrl}}/catalog?date={{date1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "MEAL": { "label": "100g almonds", "k": 579, "p": 21, "c": 22, "f": 50 }
}

### 5. GET : Get catalog for that date
GET {{baseUrl}}/catalog

### 6. PATCH : Delete a catalog entry
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/catalog
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "SK": "CATALOG#a1a1a1"
}

